        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Peierls argument: A single domain wall (two neighboring spins flipped\n  relative to each other) costs energy 2J but gains entropy k_B ln N\n  (N possible positions for the wall). For N → ∞ and any T > 0,\n  entropy wins → domain walls proliferate → long-range order destroyed."
    },
